    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d517">

                <pb facs="0670" n="571" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg571"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.00/3855: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>), <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Then in France, to the Acting Secretary
                            of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">St.
                                Jean de Luz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-11-23T19:00:00+00:00">November 23, 1936—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 23—5 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>167. Viscount Mamblas formerly of the Foreign Office and close in [apparent
                    omission] with leaders of the rebellion said in the presence of Thurston<anchor
                        n="6" xml:id="d517-f1"/> that the Havas Agency has announced the appearance
                    in Cartagena waters of a number of submarines and that as the rebels <pb
                        facs="0671" n="572" xml:id="pg572"/> have no submarines these must be
                    foreign. He is sure they are not German and therefore must be Italian. Just
                    learned, in connection with radio from the <hi rendition="#italic">Kane</hi>,
                    that there seemed to have been an explosion on the Government cruiser <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Cervantes</hi> in the harbor of Cartagena. This is a
                    possible forerunner of what most people here expect from the Italian Navy.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d517-f1" n="6" xml:id="d517-f1-content">
                <p>Walter Thurston, Counselor of Embassy in Spain, temporarily at St. Jean de Luz,
                    France.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
